  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The East Nusa Tenggara Regional Police (Polda NTT) have escalated their investigation into allegations of sexual violence involving the Kupang Regent, identified as YL. The case stems from accusations filed by a 21-year-old student, RWM. During a recent search of the regent's official residence, police officers confiscated five items to be used as evidence, including bedding and personal care products. This development comes amid widespread scrutiny and calls from various political figures, including members of the House of Representatives, demanding that the case be processed impartially regardless of political affiliation. Some political organizations have stated they would consider disciplinary actions against the regent if the allegations are proven in court. The legal process has now transitioned into the investigation phase, with potential penalties for such charges reaching up to 12 years of imprisonment.",
